# The scenes of the nested-tests deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# nested-tests.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in nested-tests.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's loan. Repaying is refused only when the loan is already repaid."
show TodaysLoan 23 29 "today's loan" --zoom 25

## Scene 2: the flat tests
note "*Flat* tests: one list, each name packing in a situation and a result."
show FlatLoanTest 10 37 "flat tests"

## Scene 3: the nested tests
note "*Nested* tests: one class per situation. First, a requested loan."
show LoanTest 12 33 "nested tests: when requested" --zoom 17-19

## Scene 4: the next situation
note "The same two questions for an approved loan, and again for a repaid one. Each group sets itself up first."
show LoanTest 35 79 "nested tests: when approved, when repaid" --zoom 39-42,62-66

## Scene 5: the gap shows
note "Run the tests against today's loan:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:nested-tests:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The report reads like a specification. A requested loan can be repaid: money back that was never lent."

## Scene 6: the fixed loan
note "The loan that allows each step only from the state before it:"
show FixedLoan 16 31 "the fixed loan" --zoom 26
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:nested-tests:test"
callout "Every situation, every question, answered. Nesting made the missing case easy to see."
